        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9c3bea8f-ab30-549d-93a6-01efb5766a49",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eardwulf, Æthelred I, Ælfwald II, Æthelwald Moll, Æthelthryth, Alhred\n- Places: Northumbria\n- Roles: kings of Northumbria\n- Topics: dynastic strife, deposition, assassination, reigns\n\nFacts:\n- Æthelred I of Northumbria was born around 762, was the son of Æthelwald Moll and Æthelthryth, and may have become king while still a child after Alhred was deposed.\n- Æthelred I was king of Northumbria from 774 to 779.\n- In 790, during dynastic strife among several noble families in Northumbria, Æthelred I attempted to have Eardwulf assassinated.\n- Æthelred I again ruled Northumbria from 790 until he was murdered on 18 April 796.\n- According to one tradition, Ælfwald II reigned as king of Northumbria after Eardwulf was deposed in 806.\n- Eardwulf may have had a second reign as king of Northumbria from 808 until perhaps 811 or 830.",
